<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ic6ebaaddad19992f4b461be5a70ced6ae97b9f84" commit="40fb6ee99c85a831c9dfa79d9858716896a1fee9" commit_message="CHROMIUM: alt-syscall: Whitelist getrandom()  Android's bionic libc recently started using getrandom(2).  BUG=b:36139813 TEST=start ARC, ssh caroline 'dmesg | grep blocked'  Change-Id: Ic6ebaaddad19992f4b461be5a70ced6ae97b9f84 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/454917 Commit-Ready: Yusuke Sato &lt;yusukes@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yusuke Sato &lt;yusukes@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="454917" owner_email="yusukes@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/17/454917/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I12ca14d592b0da8c30e4c5776bfa8643e83037ac" commit="cde4f65893eb0b8e860c54020aa45dd48e0bd6a6" commit_message="CHROMIUM: alt-syscall: Whitelist getcpu()  Android's bionic libc uses the system call to implement sched_getcpu(3), and sched_getcpu() is exported to both the framework and apps.  Since Bionic always calls getcpu() with node == NULL and tcache == NULL, returns EPERM when either of them is not NULL.  BUG=b:36139813 TEST=start ARC, ssh caroline 'dmesg | grep blocked'  Change-Id: I12ca14d592b0da8c30e4c5776bfa8643e83037ac Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/454918 Commit-Ready: Yusuke Sato &lt;yusukes@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yusuke Sato &lt;yusukes@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="454918" owner_email="yusukes@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/18/454918/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I16810cde001ff33a660035a36ab8efc027bcb105" commit="4643d02741601ad170889fce1eada0ae3c68d5f7" commit_message="bluez: migrate to /run  Since /var/run is a symlink to /run, and we want to avoid going through the stateful /var whenever possible, use the direct path.  BUG=chromium:699880 TEST=precq passes  Change-Id: I16810cde001ff33a660035a36ab8efc027bcb105 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/453418 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="453418" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/18/453418/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Ic3e0a97c452cebdaf3c4150fa1f13d750be7add2" commit="6b7fd1783ecfed940996d15fea0bfe8877d48ed1" commit_message="CHROMIUM: usb: dwc3: rockchip: don't complain about probe deferral  These may happen one or more times, depending on driver probe ordering. e.g.:    # dmesg | grep fe80   [    2.134635] rockchip-dwc3 usb@fe800000: Bailing out, error -517   [    3.423258] xhci-hcd xhci-hcd.2.auto: irq 228, io mem 0xfe800000   [    3.425367] rockchip-dwc3 usb@fe800000: USB HOST connected  Don't complain about them.  BUG=none TEST=build and boot  Change-Id: Ic3e0a97c452cebdaf3c4150fa1f13d750be7add2 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/455098 Commit-Ready: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="455098" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/98/455098/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I7298c57a920fcdc49e1fb681977d689612a48e03" commit="c1c63445fb755b08cb099bd10aea51c2126380e7" commit_message="FIXUP: CHROMIUM: drm/img-rogue: Add 1.7 IMG PowerVR Rogue driver  32-bit builds fail with the following error.  mt8173_sysconfig.c:(.text+0xb0e9e0): undefined reference to `__udivdi3'  Avoid 64 bit divide operations.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:58144 TEST=Build i386:allyesconfig or a similar configuration  Change-Id: I7298c57a920fcdc49e1fb681977d689612a48e03 Signed-off-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/455236 Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="455236" owner_email="groeck@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/36/455236/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I6d20e1d79d3944cca0647519070a5315b301ed23" commit="707586a34f1b83ca2f4c64d286f1b6576645ac9e" commit_message="CHROMIUM: Fix typo when checking dmabuf  A dmabuf of incorrect type could have been passed to the ion driver, resulting in oob writes, crashes, or other unexpected behavior. This fixes the typo that led to the issue from commit 909de5790627cb8099ab93e81a51306d113135dc, &quot;CHROMIUM: ion: add dmabuf_is_ion()&quot;  Bug:33940449, b:36117400  Change-Id: I6d20e1d79d3944cca0647519070a5315b301ed23 Signed-off-by: Robb Glasser &lt;rglasser@google.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 3ac8b4d121a6fb7a7b0e6397e27ebd2fe171b690) Signed-off-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/454999 Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="454999" owner_email="groeck@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/99/454999/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2d045134fbdd21b6b492bbeabc85ab23aef73b9a" commit="864a88e60d9dba8bc3378ca9ecd9e1720e112bad" commit_message="tcpm: anx74xx: Only connect aux to sbu when DP mode is selected  The anx74xx tcpm driver for the usb_mux_set() function is always connecting the DP aux lines to the SBU signals regardless of whether the bit flag MUX_DP_ENABLED was set or not. For CCD opertation the sbu lines are used to establish a USB connection to H1. This means that if a PD port ever attaches to a sink debug accessory, usb_mux_set would result in interrupting the USB connection being used for CCD.  In addition, the anx74xx_tcpm_mux_exit() function had a bug where the value read from ANALOG_CTRL_5 was being masked by 0x09 and then written to ANALOG_CTRL_2.  Added functions anx74xx_tcpm_mux_enter_safe_mode() and anx74xx_tcpm_mux_exit_safe_mode() so that writes to the 3 CTRL registers that are used to configure ALT_DP mode can be easily bookended.  BUG=b:36007652 BRANCH=reef TEST=Connected servo_v4 to port 0 of electro, verified that H1 console access worked. Then initiated a data role swap so that port 0 on electro was in DFP mode and the H1 console stayed connected.  - Tested with dingdong that could connect to a 4k monitor. - Tested with USB3 flash drive. - Tested Anker USBC -&gt; USBA hub  Change-Id: I2d045134fbdd21b6b492bbeabc85ab23aef73b9a Signed-off-by: Scott &lt;scollyer@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/451837 Commit-Ready: Scott Collyer &lt;scollyer@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Scott Collyer &lt;scollyer@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: S Wang &lt;swang@analogix.corp-partner.google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="451837" owner_email="scollyer@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/37/451837/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia9d3119bae3316cf1aa248ab0de82f4641551130" commit="5592582c31e8247fe77ef3250d6d87209b3ca568" commit_message="cryptohome: add public create/read link methods.  Add a method to create symbolic links and refactor the ReadLink method to be public and follow a signature similar to other public methods.  TEST=cros_workon_make --board=samus --test cryptohome BUG=b:33710917  Change-Id: Ia9d3119bae3316cf1aa248ab0de82f4641551130 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/452071 Commit-Ready: Dan Spaid &lt;dspaid@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dan Spaid &lt;dspaid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ryo Hashimoto &lt;hashimoto@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="452071" owner_email="dspaid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/71/452071/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ifbc89fa7a038a00cb2fa40629f4c491b8daa82b7" commit="e30fd56e19209ba7780d79faf408d03148082f9e" commit_message="lakitu: cleanup chromeos_startup script  Remove all parts not pertaining to Lakitu. These are things related to switching between dev and verified mode and rebuilding stateful partition. The latter operation (implemented by clobber-state script) is potentially dangerous in the context of lakitu as it can lead to data loss  BUG=b:35170131 TEST=image boots and no errors in &quot;systemctl status chromeos-startup&quot;  Change-Id: Ifbc89fa7a038a00cb2fa40629f4c491b8daa82b7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/447320 Commit-Ready: Andrey Ulanov &lt;andreyu@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Andrey Ulanov &lt;andreyu@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Aditya Kali &lt;adityakali@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="447320" owner_email="andreyu@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/20/447320/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I276b2e00e07724ba4fd556cbcccc9865d2fe21ee" commit="5e3d47dfa0f1289d3987353ce9c4dd52af52ed51" commit_message="gcc: help clang find the linker path outside the chroot.  Outside the chroot, the ${CTARGET}-ld is not in the ${PATH} so the clang could not find the linker. This patch adds the sdk/bin to the search path to help clang find the linker.  BUG=chromium:597106 TEST=./armv7a-cros-linux-gnueabi/bin/armv7a-cros-linux-gnueabi-clang      -c test.c finds the linker.  Change-Id: I276b2e00e07724ba4fd556cbcccc9865d2fe21ee Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/443408 Commit-Ready: Yunlian Jiang &lt;yunlian@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yunlian Jiang &lt;yunlian@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Caroline Tice &lt;cmtice@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="443408" owner_email="yunlian@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/08/443408/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7382c7ea0c40854a106430c157eb3e79ab309712" commit="778c5078442e52c534bf0e964a0c4c930a106195" commit_message="autotest: not raise TimeoutError in moblab_host.reboot.  This CL changes not to raise TimeoutError when moblab_host fails to restart afe in reboot.  BUG=chromium:701400 TEST=Run repair for a lab DUT using local AFE, successfully trigger repair.au.  Change-Id: I7382c7ea0c40854a1064